# * check lots

# ** 1. succeeds with valid buy-only lot data
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

$ hledger -f - check lots

# ** 2. succeeds with valid buy and sell
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -10 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $550

$ hledger -f - check lots

# ** 3. fails with invalid lots: tag value on commodity declaration
<
commodity AAPL ; lots: BADMETHOD

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

$ hledger -f - check lots
>2 /unrecognised lots: tag value/
>=1

# ** 4. check lots fails when selling more lots than available (strict mode)
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -15 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $825

$ hledger -f - check lots
>2 /Insufficient lots/
>=1

# ** 5. check lots fails when the written realised gain doesn't match the cost-basis residual
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -10 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $550
    revenues:gains    $-999

$ hledger -f - check lots
>2 /realised gain amount is wrong/
>=1

# ** 6. --ignore-lots suppresses lot errors, journal loads
<
commodity AAPL ; lots: BADMETHOD

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50} @ $50
    assets:checking

$ hledger -f - --ignore-lots print
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks                                 10 AAPL {$50} @ $50
    assets:checking

>=

# ** 7. -I also suppresses lot errors (implies --ignore-lots)
$ hledger -f - -I print
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks                                 10 AAPL {$50} @ $50
    assets:checking

>=

# ** 8. -s/--strict overrides -I, restoring lot checks
$ hledger -f - -I -s print
>2 /unrecognised lots: tag value/
>=1

# ** 9. hledger check lots overrides --ignore-lots in config (simulated via -I here)
$ hledger -f - -I check lots
>2 /unrecognised lots: tag value/
>=1

# ** 10. fails with a valueless lots: tag on an account declaration
# (account lots: tags set only the reduction method; lotfulness is declared
# on commodities)
<
account assets:stocks  ; lots:

2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

$ hledger -f - check lots
>2 /An account lots: tag sets the disposal order for lot-tracked commodities there,/
>=1

# ** 11. --ignore-lots disables lot checking but not basic lot inference,
# so entries which balance with lots enabled still balance: here the
# user-written gain posting is still set aside by the balancer.
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:checking  $-500
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -5 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $275
    revenues:gains    $-25

$ hledger -f - print -I
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:checking                            $-500
    assets:stocks                                 10 AAPL {$50}

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks                                 -5 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash                                 $275
    revenues:gains                              $-25

>=

# ** 12. With --ignore-lots, a lot transfer with a priced fee still balances:
# the fee outflow is still auto-split into transfer and dispose parts.
<
commodity ETH ; lots:

2026-01-01 buy
    assets:cash      $-20000
    assets:wallet1   10 ETH {$2000}

2026-02-01 transfer with fee
    assets:wallet1          -10 ETH
    expenses:fees           0.01 ETH @ $2100
    assets:wallet2          9.99 ETH

$ hledger -f - print -I -x
2026-01-01 buy
    assets:cash                              $-20000
    assets:wallet1                                10 ETH {$2000} @ $2000

2026-02-01 transfer with fee
    assets:wallet1                                -9.99 ETH
    assets:wallet1                                -0.01 ETH @ $2100
    expenses:fees                                  0.01 ETH @ $2100
    assets:wallet2                                 9.99 ETH

>=

# ** 13. With --ignore-lots, an acquisition with a cost basis and an elided
# counterpart still infers the transacted cost from the basis, so the
# counterpart is inferred as money, not as the lot commodity.
<
commodity gold ; lots:

2026-04-25 buy gold
    assets:cash
    assets:gold   5 gold {$10.6}

$ hledger -f - print -I -x
2026-04-25 buy gold
    assets:cash                                 $-53.0
    assets:gold                                    5 gold {$10.6} @ $10.6

>=

# ** 14. With --ignore-lots, a transfer whose lot commodity quantities don't
# add up (eg an unrecorded fee) loads, with a balancing conversion cost
# inferred; with lots enabled it is an error (see lots-errors.test).
<
commodity ABC ; lots:

2021-01-01 buy
    equity:opening   $-50
    assets:broker1    5 ABC {$10}

2021-06-01 transfer with unrecorded fee
    assets:broker1   -5 ABC
    assets:broker2   4.9 ABC
    expenses:fees    $1

$ hledger -f - print -I -x
2021-01-01 buy
    equity:opening                              $-50
    assets:broker1                                 5 ABC {$10} @@ $50

2021-06-01 transfer with unrecorded fee
    assets:broker1                                -5 ABC @ $10.00
    assets:broker2                                 4.9 ABC @ $10.00
    expenses:fees                                 $1

>=

# ** 15. --ignore-lots silences lot state errors (here, selling more than
# was acquired), letting the journal load for troubleshooting; balance
# reports show the (negative) base account balances.
<
2026-01-15 buy
    assets:stocks    10 AAPL {$50}
    assets:checking

2026-02-01 sell
    assets:stocks    -15 AAPL {$50} @ $55
    assets:cash       $825

$ hledger -f - bal -N -I
                $825  assets:cash
               $-500  assets:checking
             -5 AAPL  assets:stocks

